        "label": "Why we print the date",
        "meta": "freshness",
        "readout_title": "How we sell it",
        "pull": "Everything cardamom is worth buying for is <em>volatile</em>. That is not a figure of speech — it is the chemistry.",
        "text": "<p>The aroma sits in an oil held inside the seed: mostly cineole, which gives the cool camphor lift, and terpinyl acetate, which gives the sweetness. Both evaporate. Grinding exposes them to air; light and warmth speed it up. An intact husk slows all of it down, which is why we sell pods and never powder.</p><p>So instead of calling it fresh, we print two dates and let you judge.</p>"
      }
